      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><h3>Destination Delivery Handover for Two‑Wheeler & Motorcycle</h3>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">The handover at the final destination is the last critical control point before the vehicle changes ownership.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>It combines visual verification, mileage confirmation, and formal sign‑off to protect both the logistics provider and the recipient.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The process is performed in daylight, uses the original pickup photographs, and references the Load Receipt (LR) bilty for an accurate odometer match.</span></li></ul>
<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Inspect the vehicle under natural light to reveal any surface damage, scratches, dents, or missing accessories that may be hidden under artificial lighting.</li>
        <li>Compare the current condition with the pickup photographs taken at the point of origin. Note any discrepancies and photograph them for the record.</li>
        <li>Check that all safety equipment (helmet, lock, spare parts) listed in the dispatch manifest is present and undamaged.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Odometer Verification</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>Read the odometer and record the exact mileage on the handover sheet.</li>
        <li>Cross‑check this reading against the mileage documented on the LR bilty. Any variance greater than 5 km must be investigated and justified.</li>
        <li>Confirm that the vehicle has not been driven beyond the agreed transit distance, which could affect warranty or insurance coverage.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑off</strong>
    <ul>
        <li>The recipient reviews the inspection findings, photographs, and odometer comparison.</li>
        <li>Both parties sign the Condition Acceptance Form, acknowledging that the vehicle has been delivered in the documented state.</li>
        <li>A copy of the signed form, the inspection photos, and the LR bilty is handed to the recipient; the logistics team retains the original for audit purposes.</li>
    </ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Effective communication throughout the handover minimizes disputes. The delivery team should explain any observed wear, demonstrate key functions (lights, horn, brakes), and provide a brief maintenance checklist. All documentation—photos, mileage logs, and signed forms—must be stored digitally for at least 12 months to satisfy regulatory and insurance requirements.</p>
<p>By rigorously applying daylight re‑inspection, precise odometer verification, and a formal sign‑off, the handover process ensures transparency, protects asset value, and builds trust between the logistics provider and the end‑user.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


